module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.transparent_alias_relation_read_the_brand_keeping_peel

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data transparent_alias_relation_read_the_brand_keeping_peel: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "transparent_alias_relation_read_the_brand_keeping_peel" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**A record literal handed to a formal declared through a transparent alias of a record was refused as a mismatch between the alias and its own body.** `gunbc.econ.llm_attempt_receipt` declares `type TokenThroughput = FieldOfFractions<Nat>`, and `test.claim.llm_attempt_receipt_witness` `zero_denominator_floor_projection_returns_none` passes `FieldOfFractions { num: 1000, denom: 0 }` to `throughput_per_second_floor(t: TokenThroughput)`. The v1 compile of that witness refused with `type mismatch: expected 'Node(TokenThroughput<Primitive(Nat)>)', got 'Product(FieldOfFractions)'`. This was latent on main and blocked the floor of gunbc#12381. A fabricated refusal of correct code is the DESIGN section 5 mirror of a fabricated success.",

    "IT IS NOT SPECIFIC TO INSTANTIATION, although it was first classified as alias-through-instantiation peeling. A plain `type A = SomeRecord` receiving a `SomeRecord { .. }` literal refused the same way on main (measured with a same-module scratch probe). The generic case only makes the rendering look different, `Node(A<args>)` rather than `Primitive(A)`.",

    "THE CHAIN, per DESIGN section 6b. `v1.compiler.infer` `direct_call_structured_record_literal_resolved_type_mismatch` admits a record literal whose constructor name is `application_type_names_compatible` with the formal's name. For an alias formal, that relation's only alias arm is `type_name_transparently_aliases_to`. That arm asked `peel_nominal_alias_identity` for the alias's target name. But that peel exists to KEEP the brand: it returns the structural body stamped with the alias's own authored identity (`with_authored_identity`), so the name it yields is the alias again, and the arm answered false for every alias whose body is not a kernel primitive. The earliest unjustified boundary is that arm, not the literal site and not the peel. The arm read a projection whose contract is to hide the fact it needed.",

    "REPAIR STATUS: LANDED (gunbc#12896, quiet-hawk-702, on quiet-gull-780 ruling B; built on witty-ram-630's link (1) and link (2) from gunbc#12808). Link (1), the head relation `type_name_transparently_aliases_to`, is identity-keyed: it compares the DeclarationRef of the alias item's right-hand side head with the declaration the other side resolves to, and fails closed when no identity exists. The identity it needed now reaches v1 infer hermetically: `v1.compiler.infer_env` `TypeBinding.alias_rhs` retains the alias's RHS reference node, whose `declaration` the one writer (`v1.compiler.infer_resolve` `reference_with_declaration`, called from `v1.compiler.infer` `alias_rhs_reference`) sets in the alias's OWN env, and `alias_item_rhs_head` reads it from the declaring env found by exact module path. No spelling is re-resolved and neither the pre-resolve symbol index nor `global_bare_owner_module` is consulted. Link (2), `transparent_alias_application_at_head`, is live through the same read. The same PR found that the old spelling peel had also been silently equating two spellings of one declaration (`NonEmptyStr` and the census-qualified `std.types.NonEmptyStr`); with link (1) identity-keyed, 17 such call arguments refused in the whole corpus until `application_type_names_compatible` compared the declarations each spelling names before any peel (`same_declaration`).",

    "PINNED PROBES, ENROLLED: `test.claim.alias_head_identity_probe_witness_test` hands each probe module to the compiler through the diagnostic-census harness (`gunbc.compile_diagnostic_census`) and joins every verdict by class and subject (a TypeMismatch's subject is the type it got), so a probe refusing for another reason measures another wall. The ACCEPTED CONTROL is `test.probe.alias_head_identity_accepts_probe` (`non_generic_alias_peels`, `non_generic_alias_value`, `nat_literal_into_generic_alias`): no head mismatch on the alias's own body record; this was the red before the head identity reached v1 infer. The REFUSALS that must hold are `test.probe.alias_head_identity_refuses_probe` `different_record_into_alias` and `different_record_into_generic_alias` (a different record into each alias, refused at the head) and `wrong_field_into_record_alias` (judged per field once the head agrees), and `test.probe.alias_head_identity_homonym_probe` `wrong_homonym_into_alias` (the alias is of `alias_head_identity_hom_a`'s `WrHomRec` and receives the probe's own same-leaf `WrHomRec`). The corpus red was `test.claim.llm_attempt_receipt_witness` `zero_denominator_floor_projection_returns_none`, now accepted by the compiler; its own claim is that witness's evidence, not this row's.",

    "DECLARED FRONTIER, NOT THIS CLASS (recorded here at the manager's direction because it was first attributed to this root). `std.algebra` `ordered_ring_templates` and its siblings carry 86 advisories `declared-type inhabitance is undecidable at the list element (produced identity erased)`. The elements are ANONYMOUS record literals (`{ name: \"add\", .. }`), so the produced name is empty and the verdict is `UndecidableProducedIdentityErased`. No alias peel is involved, and this repair does not move them. TRIGGER: v1 contextual typing of an anonymous record literal from its expected element type. The design reference is the v2 work in gunbc#12740. No owner yet; it is advisory.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the floor, as a fabricated refusal at a record-literal call argument. CURRENT RUNG: structurally guaranteed for a transparent alias declared in the judging module or one of its direct imports whose RHS head carries a declaration identity; the executing evidence is the enrolled witness above, a discriminating red refused on the compile acceptance path plus an accepted control. TWO POPULATIONS STAY BELOW, each failing closed as an ordinary head mismatch rather than a fabricated success, and each with its trigger. (a) A kernel-spelled head carries no identity and is not read; TRIGGER: the one writer recording the single kernel declaration visible in scope (neat-boar-16's Int ruling). (b) An alias declared outside the judging module and its direct imports (reached only through another module's signature), and an alias chain longer than the chase fuel: `alias_item_rhs_head` finds no declaring env and answers none. TRIGGER: the declared-scope transition, after which a formal's type node carries the Node.declaration its declaring module's resolve wrote, so the alias is reached by identity from the reference rather than by env lookup in the judging scope; that transition must make this population accepted, and a probe for it is owed with it. CEILING: structurally guaranteed, once the head relation is decided on declaration identity for every transparent alias of a nominal type, generic or not.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
